WEBVTT

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.200
Finally, it's today...

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.120
My first shop tournament.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.380
Good morning.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:36.720
Good morning...

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:41.220
Mom... Look at Aichi!

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:45.100
Huh? Oh yes, he's gotten 
up quite early, hasn't he?

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.480
Here, take this to him.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.240
Vanguard Fight?

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.880
Oh, I'm sorry! I'll pick them up right now...

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.460
I see... If I recall, 
today's the tournament.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.870
That's why he's so excited.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:43.510
I'm going to be fighting 
in this tournament today.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:47.350
Aichi, brother!

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:49.570
Kamui!

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:52.050
You're entering the Shop Tournament, right?

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:56.060
So what are you waiting for? Get in 
there already, my dear brother Aichi!

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.590
Uh, right... And I'm not your brother...

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:02.360
So, where's my goddess?

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:03.280
Goddess?

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.580
I mean Emi, Brother!

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.380
Oh, I see.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.920
Emi's not with me.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.020
Okay. So she's the type that comes running 
in late to cheer you on... I got it.

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:18.410
Okay, let's go!

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.080
But she never said anything 
about showing up today...

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:32.120
What's with him?

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.520
A cosplay fighter?

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:36.280
Oooh!

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.130
What a grand stage for our great Kamui!

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.030
GS, yo!

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:43.200
E-Everyone is looking at me...

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:47.870
It's like it's not the Card 
Capital that I know...

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:52.790
Aichi!

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.570
Huh? Emi?

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:57.610
Kamui!

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:02.880
My goddess!

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:05.840
Miss Emi, you came!

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:10.340
At the next Shop Tournament...

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.190
...I'd really love it if you 
came to watch me fight!

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:16.620
Then... If I win...

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:20.400
Will you m-m-m-m-m-m-ma....

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.530
What could he have been stammering about?

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:27.500
I think he's been asking 
me every day lately...

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.530
But, why me?

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:33.290
Now, Miss Emi... This way, please!

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:35.350
U-Uh...

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:47.010
The Shop Tournament Begins

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:52.070
Everyone entering the tournament, please 
stand in front of the tournament bracket.

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:58.550
Great Kamui! Leave Miss Emi 
in our special, perfect hands!

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:00.050
SP, yo!

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:03.040
Right! If anything happens, guard her!

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.980
What is he protecting her from, I wonder?

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:10.220
When I win, you'll be my 
brother for real! Yeah!

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:18.210
Aichi...

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.680
Are you okay, Brother?

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:27.190
Get a hold of yourself, Aichi... 
Gettin' weak knees now ain't good.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:32.850
Kai...

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:38.500
Tch... Show off.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:39.860
He can hear you!

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:43.960
Kai isn't nervous at all... It's so like him.

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:46.300
Not anything like me...

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.230
Now that everyone has gathered,

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:56.960
we will now officially begin the 
Card Capital Shop Tournament!

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:03.840
Sixteen participants will hold 
a single elimination tournament,

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:07.340
and the one that remains standing 
at the end is the winner!

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:13.500
Perhaps it does not need to be said, but 
players may not receive any advice from the gallery.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.560
I will act as the referee.

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:20.060
Please follow the basic Vanguard rules.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:23.640
Anyone who breaks the 
rules may be disqualified.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:25.440
Please keep that in mind.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:29.310
Are there any questions so far?

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.090
Yes!

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:34.820
Yes... Morikawa?

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:35.840
Righto...

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:38.340
I pledge!

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:40.800
U-Uh... Would you...

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:45.720
I, the strongest Vanguard Fighter for 
Hitsue Junior High, Katsumi Morikawa,

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.090
vow to win this tournament!

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:52.900
I can see how these fights are going 
to go... But I'm a big-hearted man!

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:55.760
I'll give you all the chance right now to...

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:56.640
Hand it over!

00:06:56.970 --> 00:07:00.250
Miss Emi! I'll win it all for you!

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:03.500
And when I do, m-m-m-m-m...

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.120
You tell her, Boss!

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:06.480
YT, yo!

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.540
Give it! I haven't sung the 
tournament opening song yet!

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:12.440
Please disqualify these idiots.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:14.880
I'm not gonna let your crappy 
singing dirty my love!

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:15.180
Aww... But they're just excited, right?

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:24.210
I'd expect it from Kai,

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:27.340
but Morikawa and Kamui aren't nervous either.

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:32.480
Misaki doesn't look like it, either.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:42.230
I think I'm the only person who's nervous...

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:46.230
Can I possibly fight like this?

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:48.570
Ah... Ah...

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.820
The preliminaries will be held tournament style.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:56.340
We will split up the participants 
into four groups,

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:59.330
and the four winners from those 
groups will enter the finals.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:03.220
Now, I will announce the 
tournament match-ups!

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:05.330
I'm even more nervous now!

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:08.510
Please do me the honor, Sub-Manager.

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:11.730
Sub-Manager?

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:18.810
Manager...

00:08:21.170 --> 00:08:23.530
Please, Manager!

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:31.690
D block: Inaba/Andou    Fujino/Kai

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:33.370
Kai!

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.160
So that's the kanji for "Kai".

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:41.750
Don't think you're such hot stuff 'cause
 your name's written with a difficult kanji.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:46.000
Sub-Manager, why'd you have 
to start from D block!?

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:50.740
Manager... Could you do the rest now?

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:59.720
C bock: Kamui/Nagai    Hata/Matsumoto
B block: Misaki/Morikawa    Kawamura/Yamagami

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:01.970
I'm in C block!

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:04.060
B block...

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:06.560
A-And me?

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:12.030
A block: Aichi/Izaki   Ninja Master M/Nakanishi

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:11.240
A block...

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:18.330
I see. So I'll have to make it 
to the finals to fight Kai...

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:19.460
What's this?

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.910
I'm up against...

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:26.740
Looks like my win's in the bag...

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:30.840
Oh, right! Who am I fighting?

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:32.210
Me!

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:33.370
Izaki?

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:36.150
Ooh! Good luck, you two!

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.530
Attention, all participants...

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.740
Make sure you've checked your names.

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:44.440
Okay?

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:50.740
Now, without further ado, let's 
start the first round fights!

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:17.070
The first round of the Card Capital Shop 
Tournament will be held two fights at a time!

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:20.750
Round 1, A block fight 1:

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:24.130
Aichi Sendou vs. Yuuta Izaki!

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:29.140
B block fight 1: Katsumi 
Morikawa vs. Misaki Tokura!

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:35.110
It's the same Card Capital...

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:39.820
Well, maybe a little different...

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.560
It's the same fighting table...

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:46.120
The same opponent I always fight...

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:49.710
But for some reason, I'm still nervous!

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:53.420
I sure lucked out, getting 
Aichi as my opponent.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:57.300
Is Izaki any good?

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.900
Goddess, fights are all 
about the luck of the draw!

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:03.590
LD, yo!

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:06.150
I'll win, Miss Emi!

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:08.070
That didn't answer my question...

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:15.270
I ain't heard of the phrase "holding 
back", so you'd better get ready...

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:18.540
Shin, would you get going already?

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:21.040
Please call me Manager!

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:26.620
Now then, please place your chosen Vanguard 
card upside down on the Vanguard circle.

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:29.790
Shuffle your decks, and 
place them in the deck area.

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:35.430
After deciding who will go first, 
everyone draw five cards to their hand.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.910
L-Let's start.

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:42.330
I-I'm sorry! I'll reshuffle...

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:44.260
Fine, I'll allow it.

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:49.310
Looks like he's rubbing off on me...

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:53.400
Aichi's really, really nervous...

00:11:55.350 --> 00:11:57.830
What's the matter, Brother?

00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:00.360
You should just play like you usually do.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:06.130
Now, start the match!

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:09.020
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:15.720
Barcgal!

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:19.140
The Ironclad Dragon, Shieldon!

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:25.430
What's wrong? You start...

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:28.960
Oh... R-Right...

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:33.140
Uh oh! I don't have any grade 2s in my hand!

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:35.480
I forgot to do the redraw!

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:39.030
Oh, well...

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:40.530
I need to center myself.

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:42.730
I ride Wingal.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:50.130
With Barcgal's skill, I move 
her to the rear-guard circle.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.680
Okay, attack!

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:56.700
Oh, but the person who 
goes first can't attack...

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:58.210
My turn is over.

00:12:58.490 --> 00:13:00.280
My turn!

00:13:03.020 --> 00:13:05.840
I ride the Pterodactyl, Skyptera!

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:12.060
I attack Wingal with Skyptera!

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:14.550
Check for a drive trigger...

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:17.610
Check for a damage trigger...

00:13:18.850 --> 00:13:20.520
My turn is over.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:26.150
If I don't get a grade 2 now, 
I won't put up much of a fight.

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:27.280
Please!

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.080
Yes!

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:31.610
Gallatin!

00:13:32.070 --> 00:13:33.140
Okay.

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:35.810
I ride the Knight of Silence, Gallatin!

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.950
I call the Little Sage, Marron.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:49.200
I attack Skyptera with Gallatin, 
supported by Barcgal!

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:51.180
I defend with Ganlu!

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:56.600
Check for a drive trigger...

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:59.720
Good. Stand trigger activated!

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:02.020
Gallatin's power, +5000!

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:05.150
Plus, I stand up a unit in my rear-guard.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.310
If only I'd attacked with Marron first...

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:16.620
Check for a damage trigger...

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:19.540
I attack Skyptera with Marron!

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:21.070
I guard with Ganlu!

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:27.930
I got another of my 
ultimate cards in my hand!

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:31.590
I still can't ride them!

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:35.980
What am I doing?

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:37.760
I've been screwing up all over the place.

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:41.240
I ride the Assault Dragon, Blightops!

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:43.800
And I call another Blightops!

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:48.860
I attack Gallatin with my Vanguard Blightops!

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:52.320
Huh? But Gallatin's power is greater...

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:55.580
I-I-I knew that!

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:56.870
I just wanted to do this...

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:58.860
Check for a drive trigger...

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:03.510
How about this? Now 
Blightops's power is +5000!

00:15:03.510 --> 00:15:06.630
And I can draw a card from my deck!

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:07.960
No, you cannot.

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:12.180
Blightops is in the Tachikaze Clan.

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:14.150
Monica is from Kagero.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:18.560
Triggers do not activate unless 
they are of the same clan.

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:24.560
If you're going to make a deck with two 
clans, that should be basic knowledge.

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:26.350
My attack fails...

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:30.050
Izaki, why would...

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:33.130
I-I just made a little mistake, that's all!

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:35.410
Um... Oh well.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:39.120
I attack Marron with Blightops, 
who has the same power!

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:42.330
I defend with the Transporter 
of Good Luck, Epona!

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.300
Huh?

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:50.410
He attacked first with his Vanguard, 
and then his rear-guard?

00:15:50.410 --> 00:15:53.360
That's the same mistake I just made.

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:55.860
M-My turn's over!

00:15:56.310 --> 00:16:00.310
I see! Izaki's never entered 
this tournament before either.

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:02.810
He's nervous...

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:07.940
It's not just me... It's 
Izaki... Everyone's the same!

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:14.910
Enter the fray! I ride the 
ruler of all knights...

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:17.450
The King of Knights, Alfred!

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:21.040
Aichi!

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:27.960
Finally, the look on his face... 
That's the brother I know!

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:36.640
I call Gallatin, and the 
Yggdrasil Maiden, Elaine!

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:41.200
I attack your Vanguard Blightops 
with Gallatin, supported by Elaine!

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:44.120
I defend with Tahr!

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:49.270
How about that?

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.120
He's...

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:54.400
I attack with Alfred!

00:16:54.760 --> 00:17:01.880
In exchange for Alfred not begin able to be 
boosted, he gains +2000 for each rear-guard.

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:04.120
Total, that's power +10000!

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:06.400
What?!

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:07.960
Twin drive check!

00:17:08.350 --> 00:17:09.550
No trigger.

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:11.330
Second check!

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:12.420
No trigger.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:16.950
Checking for a damage trigger...

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:23.360
I attack Blightops with 
Marron, supported by Flogal!

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:27.230
Check for a damage trigger...

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:32.350
Aichi's nothing like he was a minute ago!

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:33.920
What happened?

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:34.950
Izaki...

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:38.210
I'm nervous, too.

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:39.200
Eh?

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:43.770
But when I realized you were 
too, I finally settled down.

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:47.910
When I did that, it became 
fun, just like it usually is!

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:49.910
Fun?

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:53.650
Oh... That's right...

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:56.680
Vanguard fights should be fun!

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:57.540
Yeah!

00:17:57.540 --> 00:17:58.610
Let's go!

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:03.320
I ride the Tyrant Deathrex!

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:13.280
I call the Wyvern Guard, Barri, Skyptera, 
and the Dragon Dancer, Monica!

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:19.410
I attack Alfred with Barri, 
supported by Skyptera!

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:21.650
I defend with Marron!

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:23.930
Not gonna pass, huh?

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:25.970
I'm not done yet!

00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:26.530
Yeah!

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:29.550
I attack Alfred with Deathrex!

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:33.250
Deathrex gains +5000 power while attacking!

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:35.760
Twin drive check!

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:38.650
And again!

00:18:39.020 --> 00:18:40.640
Trigger activated!

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:43.200
I give power +5000 to Blightops!

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:46.890
And Deathrex's critical +1!

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:50.810
Check for a damage trigger...

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:52.320
That's the first.

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:55.190
That's the second...

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:58.630
When Deathrex's attack is successful,

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:00.910
one of the rear-guard must by retired.

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:06.580
But, using Skyptera's ability, 
by paying a cost of 1,

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.080
it can be returned to the hand when dropped.

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:13.690
I attack Alfred with Blightops, 
supported by Monica!

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:19.880
I guard with the Future Knight, Llew!

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:26.940
Turn over.

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:33.830
Yup!

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:40.280
I move Marron to the back, 
and Flogal to the front.

00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:43.450
Plus, I call Gancelot!

00:19:45.230 --> 00:19:47.030
I retire Flogal.

00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:51.910
I attack Deathrex with Gallatin, 
supported by Elaine!

00:19:55.780 --> 00:19:58.000
I have 3 damage...

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.540
Okay... I guard with Skyptera!

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.850
And intercept with Blightops!

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:14.940
I attack Deathrex with Alfred!

00:20:19.390 --> 00:20:22.860
If I let this attack through, 
and guard the next...

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:25.240
Twin drive check...

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:27.280
Critical trigger!

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:30.680
His critical is still only 2!

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:32.650
Second check...

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:34.580
What?!

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:38.090
Power +10000, and critical 3?!

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:40.990
Damage trigger...

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:42.670
...triple check...

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:53.020
I lost.

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:58.230
The winner of the first fight 
in Round 1, from A block, is:

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:00.900
Aichi Sendou!

00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:04.530
Thank you, Izaki!

00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:07.320
I was nervous, but it was a lot of fun.

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.310
Me, too.

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:11.180
I-I lost...

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:14.980
The best player in Hitsue 
Junior High, I, have lost!

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:18.670
It's because the horoscope this 
morning said I'd be unlucky 13!

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:20.660
Luck's not with me today, again!

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:23.050
B block's winner: Misaki Tokura!

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:29.840
We... We'd expect nothing 
less from our brother, right?

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:38.640
Misaki's expression is exactly 
the same, even after she won.

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:43.520
She really is totally different 
from me, a bundle of nerves...

00:21:50.590 --> 00:21:51.890
Misaki...

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:56.540
Yeah... This is the Shop Tournament!

00:21:59.700 --> 00:22:00.540
Good.

00:22:04.820 --> 00:22:06.110
If I can win one more time,

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:08.560
then I'll get to go to the finals!

00:22:08.560 --> 00:22:12.970
And if I do that... I'll get a
 chance to fight Kai!

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:54.420
It was so nerve-wrecking being in the 
first fight at the tournament!

00:23:54.420 --> 00:23:56.580
Yeah, seriously! But it was a lot of fun!

00:23:56.810 --> 00:23:59.660
My horoscope was just awful.

00:23:59.660 --> 00:24:00.620
What's your sign, Morikawa?

00:24:00.860 --> 00:24:03.620
Hey, Aichi... Your next opponent...

00:24:03.620 --> 00:24:04.890
I-It's that guy...

00:24:04.890 --> 00:24:07.830
A samurai? A ninja? Who is he?!

00:24:07.830 --> 00:24:10.300
Next time: Enter the Ninja Fighter!

00:24:10.300 --> 00:24:12.030
Picture it, Aichi!

00:24:12.030 --> 00:24:15.140
Earth Art! Fire Art! 
Shurikens and smoke bombs!

00:24:15.140 --> 00:24:17.900
Sorry 'bout that! Can I have your autograph?
